  "text_md": "Assessment of IUCN threat category and present.... ***July-December 2022***\n\n## Table.1 : Previous and current status of A. desertorum in Indian desert.\n\n## Occurrence localities reported in previous work Occurrence localities reported during current work\n\n|Occurrence locality|Authors|||Current status reported during||\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|||||field survey 2016-2020||\n|Mandore, Jodhpur|Bhandari, 203, 294,1293 (JAC)|||Not present||\n|Devikot, Jaisalmer|Blatter&Hallberg, 3341 (BLAT); Tiwari 867 (BSJO)|||Not present||\n|Vinjorai, Jaisalmer|Blatter&Hallberg, 3344 (BLAT);|||Not present||\n|Kotda, Jodhpur|Blatter&Hallberg, 3345 (BLAT);|||Not present||\n|Badka, Jodhpur|Blatter&Hallberg, 3346, 3347 (BLAT);|||Not present||\n|Not reported Table 2 : Sheet of IUCN Criteria-A.|Not reported|||Akal wood fossil park, Jaisalmer||\n|Use of the criteria A A. Population reduction||Critically Endangered Declines measured over the longer of 10 years or 3 generations|Endangered||Vulnerable|\n|A1||≥ 90%|≥ 70%||≥ 50%|\n|A2, A3 & A4||≥ 80% √|≥ 50%||≥ 30%|\n\nA2: Population reduction observed, estimated, inferred, or suspected in the past where the causes of reduction may not have ceased **OR** may not be understood **OR** may not be reversible, based on and specifying any of the following Tick right sign. others\n\n(a) direct observation √\n(b) an index of abundance appropriate to the taxon X\n(c) a decline in area of occupancy (AOO), extent of occurrence (EOO) √ and/or habitat quality\n(d) actual or potential levels of exploitation X\n(e) effects of introduced taxa, hybridization, pathogens, pollutants, X competitors or parasites.\n## IUCN AssessmentCR/A2ac\n\n**Table 3 : Sheet of IUCN Criteria-B**\n\n|Use of the criteria B|Critically Endangered|Endangered|Vulnerable|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|B. Geographic range|Geographic range in the form of either B1 (extent of occurrence) AND/OR B2 (area of occupancy)|||\n|B1. Extent of occurrence (EOO)|< 100 km²|< 5,000 km²|< 20,000 km²|\n|B2. Area of occupancy (AOO)|< 10 km² √|< 500 km²|< 2,000 km²|\n|B1 OR B2. (a)|= 1 √|≤ 5|≤ 10|\n\nSeverely fragmented, OR Number of locations\n",
